# text = Great men are seldom over scrupulous in the arrangement of their attire ; the operation of shaving , dressing , and coffee-imbibing was soon performed ; and , in another hour , Mr . Pickwick , with his portmanteau in his hand , his telescope in his greatcoat pocket , and his note-book in his waistcoat , ready for the reception of any discoveries worthy of being noted down , had arrived at the coach-stand in St . Martin's-le-Grand said Mr . Pickwick shouted a strange specimen of the human race , in a sackcloth coat , and apron of the same , who , with a brass label and number round his neck , looked as if he were catalogued in some collection of rarities .
