# text = The young ladies laughed very heartily , and the old one tried to look amiable , but couldn't manage it said Miss Wardle to Mr . Tupman , with an air of gentle commiseration , as if animal spirits were contraband , and their possession without a permit a high crime and misdemeanour replied Mr . Tupman , not exactly making the sort of reply that was expected from him said Miss Wardle , rather dubiously said Mr . Tupman , in his blandest manner , touching the enchanting Rachael's wrist with one hand , and gently elevating the bottle with the other Mr . Tupman looked most impressive ; and Rachael expressed her fear that more guns were going off , in which case , of course , she should have required support again whispered their affectionate aunt to Mr . Tupman replied the ready Pickwickian , with a passionate glance said Mr . Tupman , with an air of indifference inquired Mr . Tupman , who had not precisely made up his mind to say anything at all Mr . Tupman had no objection to earning the reputation at so cheap a rate : so he looked very knowing , and smiled mysteriously said the admiring Rachael said Mr . Tupman , who had not the slightest notion himself said the amiable aunt , sinking her voice still lower Here the affectionate relative heaved a deep sigh , and shook her head despondingly whispered Miss Emily Wardle to her sister replied Isabella However well deserved this piece of retaliation might have been , it was as vindictive a one as could well have been resorted to .
