# text = An old eight-day clock , of solemn and sedate demeanour , ticked gravely in one corner ; and a silver watch , of equal antiquity , dangled from one of the many hooks which ornamented the dresser said the old gentleman inquiringly , when his guests had been washed , mended , brushed , and brandied replied Mr . Pickwick and the party having traversed several dark passages , and being joined by Mr . Tupman , who had lingered behind to snatch a kiss from Emma , for which he had been duly rewarded with sundry pushings and scratchings , arrived at the parlour door said their hospitable host , throwing it open and stepping forward to announce them Several guests who were assembled in the old parlour rose to greet Mr . Pickwick and his friends upon their entrance ; and during the performance of the ceremony of introduction , with all due formalities , Mr . Pickwick had leisure to observe the appearance , and speculate upon the characters and pursuits , of the persons by whom he was surrounded -- a habit in which he , in common with many other great men , delighted to indulge .
