# text = Wardle looked on in silent wonder said Mr . Pickwick and the stranger grasped Mr . Wardle's hand with all the fervour of a close intimacy of many years , and then stepped back a pace or two as if to take a full survey of his face and figure , and then shook hands with him again , if possible , more warmly than before said Mr . Pickwick , with a smile in which benevolence struggled with surprise replied the stranger Mr . Pickwick was sufficiently versed in the stranger's system of stenography to infer from this rapid and disjointed communication that he had , somehow or other , contracted an acquaintance with the All-Muggletons , which he had converted , by a process peculiar to himself , into that extent of good-fellowship on which a general invitation may be easily founded .
