# text = The Pickwickians had no sooner dismounted than they were surrounded by a branch mob of the honest and independent , who forthwith set up three deafening cheers , which being responded to by the main body ( for it's not at all necessary for a crowd to know what they are cheering about ), swelled into a tremendous roar of triumph , which stopped even the red-faced man in the balcony shouted the mob , in conclusion screamed the little fugleman in the balcony , and out shouted the mob again , as if lungs were cast-iron , with steel works roared the honest and independent echoed Mr . Pickwick , taking off his hat roared the crowd shouted Mr . Pickwick
