# text = As these taunts were accompanied with invidious comparisons between Mr . Pickwick and an aged ram , and several witticisms of the like nature ; and as they moreover rather tended to convey reflections upon the honour of an innocent lady , Mr . Pickwick's indignation was excessive ; but as silence was proclaimed at the moment , he contented himself by scorching the mob with a look of pity for their misguided minds , at which they laughed more boisterously than ever roared the mayor's attendants said the mayor , with an air of pomp befitting his lofty station .
