# text = At all these encounters , Horatio Fizkin , Esquire , of Fizkin Lodge , and his friends , waxed fierce and furious ; until at last Horatio Fizkin , Esquire , of Fizkin Lodge , begged to ask his opponent , the Honourable Samuel Slumkey , of Slumkey Hall , whether that band played by his consent ; which question the Honourable Samuel Slumkey declining to answer , Horatio Fizkin , Esquire , of Fizkin Lodge , shook his fist in the countenance of the Honourable Samuel Slumkey , of Slumkey Hall ; upon which the Honourable Samuel Slumkey , his blood being up , defied Horatio Fizkin , Esquire , to mortal combat .
