# text = As the coach rolls swiftly past the fields and orchards which skirt the road , groups of women and children , piling the fruit in sieves , or gathering the scattered ears of corn , pause for an instant from their labour , and shading the sun-burned face with a still browner hand , gaze upon the passengers with curious eyes , while some stout urchin , too small to work , but too mischievous to be left at home , scrambles over the side of the basket in which he has been deposited for security , and kicks and screams with delight .
