# text = Nathaniel Pipkin was a harmless , inoffensive , good-natured being , with a turned-up nose , and rather turned-in legs , a cast in his eye , and a halt in his gait ; and he divided his time between the church and his school , verily believing that there existed not , on the face of the earth , so clever a man as the curate , so imposing an apartment as the vestry-room , or so well-ordered a seminary as his own .
