# text = The gamekeeper having been coaxed and feed , and having , moreover , eased his mind by ' punching ' the head of the inventive youth who had first suggested the use of the machine , Mr . Pickwick was placed in it , and off the party set ; Wardle and the long gamekeeper leading the way , and Mr . Pickwick in the barrow , propelled by Sam , bringing up the rear said Mr . Pickwick , when they had got half across the first field said Wardle said Mr . Pickwick , resolutely said the wretched Winkle replied Mr . Pickwick reasoned Winkle replied Mr . Pickwick growled the long man said poor Winkle , turning his gun - stock uppermost said Mr . Weller ; and on they went again said Mr . Pickwick , after they had gone a few yards farther said Wardle said Mr . Pickwick said Mr . Tupman , in a tone of great alarm said Mr . Pickwick said the long gamekeeper Mr . Tupman , with the most obliging haste , placed his piece in the position required , and the party moved on again ; the two amateurs marching with reversed arms , like a couple of privates at a royal funeral .
