# text = His first act was to bolt the door on the inside ; his second , to polish his head and countenance very carefully with a cotton handkerchief ; his third , to place his hat , with the cotton handkerchief in it , on the nearest chair ; and his fourth , to produce from the breast-pocket of his coat a short truncheon , surmounted by a brazen crown , with which he beckoned to Mr . Pickwick with a grave and ghost-like air .
