# text = Desiring Mr . Pickwick to walk to the upper end of the little apartment , and holding his hand upon the half-closed door , that he might be able to effect an immediate escape , in case there was the least tendency to a display of hostilities , Mr . Nupkins expressed his readiness to hear the communication , whatever it might be said Mr . Pickwick interrupted Sam said Mr . Pickwick replied Mr . Weller said Mr . Pickwick added Mr . Pickwick , as he saw that Mr . Nupkins was about to offer a very indignant interruption said Mr . Nupkins , closing the door said the excited Mr . Pickwick said Mr . Nupkins , turning very red , and altering his whole manner directly said Sam said the magistrate said Sam said Mr . Pickwick , replying to the magistrate's look of amazement Mr . Pickwick proceeded to pour into the horror-stricken ear of Mr . Nupkins , an abridged account of all Mr . Jingle's atrocities .
