# text = Mixed up with the pleasure and joy of the occasion , are the many regrets at quitting home , the tears of parting between parent and child , the consciousness of leaving the dearest and kindest friends of the happiest portion of human life , to encounter its cares and troubles with others still untried and little known -- natural feelings which we would not render this chapter mournful by describing , and which we should be still more unwilling to be supposed to ridicule .
