# text = Pickwick had not spoken in a very loud tone , but she understood him at once , and drank off a full glass of wine to his long life and happiness ; after which the worthy old soul launched forth into a minute and particular account of her own wedding , with a dissertation on the fashion of wearing high-heeled shoes , and some particulars concerning the life and adventures of the beautiful Lady Tollimglower , deceased ; at all of which the old lady herself laughed very heartily indeed , and so did the young ladies too , for they were wondering among themselves what on earth grandma was talking about .
