# text = He walked away ; and Mr . Pickwick's countenance resumed its customary benign expression said Mr . Pickwick , who was stationed with the old lady at the top of the dance , and had already made four false starts , in his excessive anxiety to commence said Wardle Up struck the two fiddles and the one harp , and off went Mr . Pickwick into hands across , when there was a general clapping of hands , and a cry of said Mr . Pickwick , who was only brought to , by the fiddles and harp desisting , and could have been stopped by no other earthly power , if the house had been on fire cried a dozen voices added Mr . Tupman exclaimed that gentleman , emerging with his pretty companion from the corner ; as he did so , it would have been hard to tell which was the redder in the face , he or the young lady with the black eyes said Mr .
