# text = It by no means follows that because a man is a sexton , and constantly surrounded by the emblems of mortality , therefore he should be a morose and melancholy man ; your undertakers are the merriest fellows in the world ; and I once had the honour of being on intimate terms with a mute , who in private life , and off duty , was as comical and jocose a little fellow as ever chirped out a devil-may-care song , without a hitch in his memory , or drained off a good stiff glass without stopping for breath .
