# text = Books of practice , heaps of papers , and opened letters , were scattered over the table , without any attempt at order or arrangement ; the furniture of the room was old and rickety ; the doors of the book-case were rotting in their hinges ; the dust flew out from the carpet in little clouds at every step ; the blinds were yellow with age and dirt ; the state of everything in the room showed , with a clearness not to be mistaken , that Mr . Serjeant Snubbin was far too much occupied with his professional pursuits to take any great heed or regard of his personal comforts .
