# text = Dodson & amp ; Fogg's case as much harm as he conveniently could , and saying just as little respecting Mr . Pickwick as might be , which was precisely the object he had had in view all along said Serjeant Snubbin said Serjeant Buzfuz , putting in the two letters to be read Serjeant Snubbin then addressed the jury on behalf of the defendant ; and a very long and a very emphatic address he delivered , in which he bestowed the highest possible eulogiums on the conduct and character of Mr . Pickwick ; but inasmuch as our readers are far better able to form a correct estimate of that gentleman's merits and deserts , than Serjeant Snubbin could possibly be , we do not feel called upon to enter at any length into the learned gentleman's observations .
