# text = Winkle had got inside ; and Mr . Pickwick was preparing to follow him , when Sam Weller came up to his master , and whispering in his ear , begged to speak to him , with an air of the deepest mystery said Mr . Pickwick replied Sam inquired Mr . Pickwick rejoined Sam said Mr . Pickwick replied Sam As Sam spoke , he pointed to that part of the coach door on which the proprietor's name usually appears ; and there , sure enough , in gilt letters of a goodly size , was the magic name of PICKWICK exclaimed Mr . Pickwick , quite staggered by the coincidence said Sam , again directing his master's attention to the coach door said Mr . Pickwick exclaimed Sam , perfectly aghast at the coolness with which Mr . Pickwick prepared to ensconce himself inside said Mr . Pickwick said Mr . Weller , who had expected that at least he would have been commissioned to challenge the guard and the coachman to a pugilistic encounter on the spot replied Mr . Pickwick eagerly muttered Sam to himself , as he turned away Mr . Weller shook his head gravely ; and it is worthy of remark , as an illustration of the manner in which he took this circumstance to heart , that he did not speak another word until the coach reached the Kensington turnpike .
