# text = ' Mornin ', old friend ,' said Sam replied the groom , casting a surly look at Sam said Sam replied the ill-tempered groom said Sam The surly groom looked surlier still at this , but not sufficiently so to produce any effect upon Sam , who immediately inquired , with a countenance of great anxiety , whether his master's name was not Walker said the groom said the groom replied Sam said Sam , as the groom wheeled in the barrow , and prepared to shut the gate said the surly groom , bolting one half of the gate rejoined Sam . ' It ' ud be worth a life's board wages at least , to you , and In reply to this , the groom waxing very wroth , muttered a desire to damage somebody's person ; but disappeared without carrying it into execution , slamming the door angrily after him , and wholly unheeding Sam's affectionate request , that he would leave him a lock of his hair before he went .
