# text = While these observations were being exchanged between Mr . Bob Sawyer and Mr . Benjamin Allen ; and while the boy in the gray livery , marvelling at the unwonted prolongation of the dinner , cast an anxious look , from time to time , towards the glass door , distracted by inward misgivings regarding the amount of minced veal which would be ultimately reserved for his individual cravings ; there rolled soberly on through the streets of Bristol , a private fly , painted of a sad green colour , drawn by a chubby sort of brown horse , and driven by a surly-looking man with his legs dressed like the legs of a groom , and his body attired in the coat of a coachman .
