# text = Mr . Martin , who was a man of few words and possessed but little power of eloquence or persuasion , submitted to this operation with a very calm and agreeable expression of countenance , for some seconds ; finding , however , that it threatened speedily to lead to a result which would place it beyond his power to claim any wages , board or otherwise , in all time to come , he muttered an inarticulate remonstrance and felled Mr . Benjamin Allen to the ground .
