# text = Allen deliberately crushed his spectacles beneath the heel of his boot , and having picked up the pieces , and put them into three separate pockets , folded his arms , bit his lips , and looked in a threatening manner at the bland features of Mr . Pickwick inquired Mr . Benjamin Allen at length interrupted the old lady said the surly man , coming forward Mr . Martin , who , as it has already appeared , was a man of few words , looked at Sam Weller , nodded his head , and growled forth Mr . Weller , who was never proud , gave a smile of friendly recognition as his eyes encountered those of the surly groom , and admitted in courteous terms , that he had exclaimed Mr . Ben Allen cried Bob Sawyer fiercely said Ben Allen added Mr . Bob Sawyer observed the old lady remarked Martin urged Mr . Pickwick , as Mr . Ben Allen fell into a chair that patients were bled in , and gave way to his pocket - handkerchief added Mr . Pickwick , hastily checking himself said Mr . Benjamin Allen mildly observed Mr . Pickwick , looking round added that gentleman , his colour mounting as he spoke I wish to make a wery few remarks in addition to wot has been put for'ard by the honourable gen'l'm'n as has jist give over ,' said Mr . Weller , stepping forth interposed Mr . Pickwick replied Sam , ' but merely this here .
