# text = Weller departed on his errand , and presently returned to say that there was only a gentleman with one eye ; and that he and the landlord were drinking a bowl of bishop together said Mr . Pickwick observed Mr . Weller , as he led the way The individual to whom this observation referred , was sitting at the upper end of the room when Mr . Pickwick entered , and was smoking a large Dutch pipe , with his eye intently fixed on the round face of the landlord ; a jolly-looking old personage , to whom he had recently been relating some tale of wonder , as was testified by sundry disjointed exclamations of and other expressions of astonishment which burst spontaneously from his lips , as he returned the fixed gaze of the one-eyed man said the one-eyed man to Mr . Pickwick replied Mr . Pickwick , as the waiter placed a small decanter of brandy , and some hot water before him .
