# text = Mr . Bob Sawyer was seated , not in the dickey , but on the roof of the chaise , with his legs as far asunder as they would conveniently go , wearing Mr . Samuel Weller's hat on one side of his head , and bearing , in one hand , a most enormous sandwich , while , in the other , he supported a goodly-sized case-bottle , to both of which he applied himself with intense relish , varying the monotony of the occupation by an occasional howl , or the interchange of some lively badinage with any passing stranger .
