# text = It so happened that Mr . Winkle , senior , instead of being deeply engaged in reading the letter , as Mr . Bob Sawyer thought , chanced to be looking over the top of it at no less a person than Mr . Bob Sawyer himself ; rightly conjecturing that the face aforesaid was made in ridicule and derision of his own person , he fixed his eyes on Bob with such expressive sternness , that the late Mr . Grimaldi's lineaments gradually resolved themselves into a very fine expression of humility and confusion inquired Mr . Winkle , senior , after an awful silence replied Bob , With no remains of the clown about him , save and except the extreme redness of his cheeks said Mr .
