# text = Winkle , senior , looking contemptuously at Ben Allen , who was shaking his head profoundly All this time , Bob Sawyer had been nudging Mr . Ben Allen to say something on the right side ; Ben accordingly now burst , without the slightest preliminary notice , into a brief but impassioned piece of eloquence said Mr . Ben Allen , staring at the old gentleman , out of a pair of very dim and languid eyes , and working his right arm vehemently up and down retorted Mr . Winkle , senior With these words the old gentleman took up the candle-stick and opening the room door , politely motioned towards the passage said Mr . Pickwick , setting his teeth close together to keep down his choler ; for he felt how important the effect might prove to his young friend calmly replied Mr . Winkle , senior Mr . Pickwick walked with angry strides into the street .
