# text = No man never see a dead donkey ' cept the gen'l'm'n in the black silk smalls as know'd the young asked Bob Sawyer replied Sam Expatiating upon this learned and remarkable theory , and citing many curious statistical and other facts in its support , Sam Weller beguiled the time until they reached Dunchurch , where a dry postboy and fresh horses were procured ; the next stage was Daventry , and the next Towcester ; and at the end of each stage it rained harder than it had done at the beginning remonstrated Bob Sawyer , looking in at the coach window , as they pulled up before the door of the Saracen's Head , Towcester said Mr . Pickwick , just awakening from a nap returned Bob Bob did look dampish , inasmuch as the rain was streaming from his neck , elbows , cuffs , skirts , and knees ; and his whole apparel shone so with the wet , that it might have been mistaken for a full suit of prepared oilskin said Bob , giving himself a shake and casting a little hydraulic shower around , like a Newfoundland dog just emerged from the water interposed Ben remarked Sam Weller , coming to assist in the conference said Sam , addressing his master
