# text = ' This evening , Sir , at seven o'clock ,' said Job , taking one step forward replied Job answered Job said Perker , addressing Mr . Pickwick aloud interposed Jingle , with great firmness continued Perker , without noticing Jingle's observation said Jingle hastily Here Mr . Jingle paused , and striking the crown of his hat with great violence , passed his hand over his eyes , and sat down said Job , advancing a few paces said Job , with energy said Mr . Pickwick , who had been bestowing a score or two of frowns upon Perker , to stop his summary of benefits conferred , which the little attorney obstinately disregarded Mr . Jingle smiled at this sally , but looked rather foolish notwithstanding ; so Mr . Pickwick changed the subject by saying inquired Jingle Jingle shook his head exclaimed Mr . Pickwick said Job , with a cunning look just lurking in the corners of his eyes said Mr . Pickwick , smiling said Job said Perker , sealing a letter which he had just finished writing replied Job said the little man , laughing As Perker said this , he looked towards the door , with an evident desire to render the leave-taking as brief as possible .
