# text = So saying , he put his umbrella under his arm , drew off his right glove , and extended the hand of reconciliation to that most indignant gentleman ; who , thereupon , thrust his hands beneath his coat tails , and eyed the attorney with looks of scornful amazement cried Perker , at this moment said Mr . Pickwick said the little attorney , who had been in a state of nervous apprehension during the whole interview replied Mr . Pickwick hastily Dodson turned round , bent his head meekly , and smiled repeated Mr . Pickwick , almost breathless exclaimed Dodson reiterated Fogg continued Mr . Pickwick replied Dodson rejoined Fogg , slapping his pocket -- perhaps by accident said Mr . Pickwick , attempting to call up a sneer for the first time in his life , and failing most signally in so doing said Mr . Pickwick , turning upon Fogg with a fierceness of gesture which caused that person to retreat towards the door with great expedition said Dodson , who , though he was the biggest man of the party , had prudently entrenched himself behind Fogg , and was speaking over his head with a very pale face said Fogg , falling back a little more as he spoke ; to the evident relief of his partner , who by these means was gradually getting into the outer office continued Mr . Pickwick , resuming the thread of his discourse interposed Perker rejoined Mr . Pickwick said Perker , in a most conciliatory tone Mr . Lowten , with a distant giggle , replied in the affirmative cried the little man , pushing Dodson & amp ; Fogg , nothing loath , out of the office said Dodson , looking towards Mr . Pickwick , as he put on his hat said Fogg continued Mr . Pickwick , taking not the least notice of the threats that were addressed to him cried Mr . Pickwick , running to the stair-head , as the two attorneys descended shouted Mr . Pickwick , breaking from Lowten and Perker , and thrusting his head out of the staircase window .
