# text = The testy manner in which the hearty old gentleman uttered this last sentence was not wholly unwarranted ; for Mr . Pickwick's face had settled down into an expression of blank amazement and perplexity , quite curious to behold were the first broken words that issued from the lips of the confounded gentleman replied Wardle said Mr . Pickwick , ruminating replied the choleric old gentleman added Wardle , after a moment's hesitation inquired Mr . Pickwick rejoined Wardle interposed Perker , who had accompanied this dialogue with sundry twitchings of his watch-chain , vindictive rubbings of his nose , and other symptoms of impatience said Wardle remarked Perker rejoined the old gentleman said Mr . Pickwick replied Wardle said Perker answered Wardle said Perker , looking from the musing face of Mr . Pickwick to the eager countenance of Wardle , and taking several consecutive pinches of his favourite stimulant said Wardle , looking at Mr . Pickwick replied that gentleman said Perker , rising and pushing his chair back said Wardle , hardly knowing whether to smile or be offended returned Perker
